{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"task based asynchronous pattern task based asynchronous pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md","fileName":"Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"task based asynchronous pattern task based asynchronous pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md","fileName":"Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern","heading":"Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Task-Based Asynchronous Pattern represents an operation with a method that returns `Task` or `Task<T>`, allowing completion, results, cancellation, and faults to travel through one composable object. The method normally uses an `Async` suffix and begins useful work without blocking the caller for its full duration.\n\nCompiler-generated `async` methods are the common implementation, but a method can also construct the task contract manually. Either way, callers should be able to await the operation and observe its terminal state without learning how its internal work was scheduled.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Paral